-- title:
--   Unramified level sets of the modular unit on the j-chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a non-zero natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image, under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$, assumed non-zero, have as its Laurent series the coefficientwise image of $q^{-1}$ times the power series $j$-numerator, and let $R = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ be the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $v \in R$ have as its Laurent series either the coefficientwise image of $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ or $p^{12}$ times the inverse of that image. Then there is a non-zero $c_0' \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ such that for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ whose image in $\mathbb{Q}[X]$ is irreducible and which does not divide $c_0'$, and every prime ideal $Q$ of $R/(g(v))$ whose contraction to $A$ is $(0)$, the $A$-algebra $R/(g(v))$ is unramified at $Q$.
--
--   This is the generic-fibre unramifiedness statement for the fibres of the modular unit $\Delta(\tau)/\Delta(p\tau)$ on the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring above $p$ in $\mathbb{Z}[\zeta_p]$: away from a finite set of critical values, encoded by the divisors of $c_0'$, the level set $g(v) = 0$ is unramified over $A$ at primes lying over the generic point. It feeds the construction of finite étale quotients of these level sets in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
